{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/861738-growlscampaigncraft-abyssals-and-linguistics-brainstorm-ideas-welcome","id":861738,"title":"[GrowlsCampaignCraft] Abyssals and Linguistics - Brainstorm - IDEAS WELCOME","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-08T04:38:20-07:00","id":861738,"title":"[GrowlsCampaignCraft] Abyssals and Linguistics - Brainstorm - IDEAS WELCOME","content":"Right.<br /> I'm about to craft a fitting antagonist for my players, and I realized that he would have to be their missing Circle member, just as an Abyssal.<br /> And he would be the member who was a Twilight.<br /> <br /> In this case, he would be a Daybreak, and to break with form, I decided that he would get Linguistics as his focus abilty.<br /> <br /> So. What sorts of effects would Abyssal Linguistics be able to pull off?<br /> I realize I could just make black Solar charms, but come on. Let's get creative.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T05:57:51-07:00","id":861766,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> The Dead's Language - Being able to communicate with and command (even mindless) undead, regardless of their languages in life.<br /> <br /> Rhetoric of the Void - Effects that give bonuses to demoralizing or depressive social interactions that seeks to convince their targets that they are weak and insignificant.<br /> <br /> Blasphemous Words - Spoken or written words that sin against the nature of Creation, tearing it apart and dealing physical damage.<br /> <br /> The Black Rune - Signs or symbols that spread Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> Mouthpiece of Anguish - Charms that interact with spreading nihilistic or depressive messages through poetry or fiction.<br /> <br /> I'm too lazy to look in the Abyssal books from 1e and 2e, but I'm sure there are many good ideas there too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:05:51-07:00","id":861771,"title":"","content":"How about a charm that lets you encode &quot;written&quot; social attacks in various scenes of death/destruction. Something like &quot;the blood splatters from the massacre perfectly spell out a death poem&quot; or even just &quot;The embalmed corpse in the crypt and the withered flowers around him convince you that there is beauty and peace in death&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:18:15-07:00","id":861779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://boneandebony.livejournal.com/tag/linguistics\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://l-stat.livejournal.net/img/og_image.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://boneandebony.livejournal.com/tag/linguistics\" target=\"_blank\"> boneandebony, posts by tag: linguistics - LiveJournal </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://boneandebony.livejournal.com/tag/linguistics\" target=\"_blank\"> http://boneandebony.livejournal.com/tag/linguistics </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Interesting posts by tag: linguistics. Read on the LiveJournal blog boneandebony </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Three Abyssal Linguistics Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T07:05:12-07:00","id":861804,"title":"","content":"Woah there... you have 4 Solar PCs and the one caste that wasn't taken was Twilight? That's pretty shocking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T07:24:29-07:00","id":861818,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Abyssal_Linguistics_Charms\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a list of 2e Abyssal Linguistics.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T08:10:35-07:00","id":861844,"title":"","content":"Annoying angsty poetry!<br /> <br /> More seriously, social influence-enhancing linguistics, as long as the influence is to degrade a positive one, or to enhance something like &quot;This world is not worth saving [Principle]&quot;<br /> <br /> Would something like speaking through undead work this way? Hungry ghosts delivering messages for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:24:45-07:00","id":862142,"title":"","content":"Record the Intimacies of the dying in an unholy missive, ensuring they will rise as a ghost upon death. So long as the text is intact, it serves as the ghost's anchor and their intimacies become near-inviolate. Upgrade(?): The truth of the registered words is immediately obvious to any who read the missive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:56:15-07:00","id":862169,"title":"","content":"Maybe linguistics charms to cut off large groups of people from others? Forcing them all to speak Old Realm or a &quot;dead&quot; language that barely anyone uses anymore. Everyone in the village can still speak with one another, but not with visitors, merchants, the tax-man from the Realm, or even the monks come to help them with their bizarre curse.<br /> <br /> Going into a fugue state where you allow the mad whispers of the Neverborn to channel themselves through your pen, creating a book that drives readers mad or nihilistic. Even you yourself are not immune to your dread treatise, though you are only temporarily stricken, whereas a mortal is doomed for life. <br /> <br /> Being able to deliver powerful Inspire actions towards negative moods. Being able to write a poem so innately enraging, that even those who simply recite it aloud can deliver its full effects to all who hear. <br /> <br /> Being able to create an inkwell that fills itself with the memories of the dead, letting mortals dip quills into its reservoir to communicate with beings in the Underworld. <br /> <br /> I'm imagining a lot less Abyssal Directly Does Thing and a lot more Abyssal Creates Tool That Mortal Can Use (and not a nice one). Why directly be responsible for the 100 Theses that drive thousands of mortals away from the Immaculate Philosophy, when you can be the Muse for someone else to do so? Corrupt! Inspire! Drive mad with grief! Carry the wishes and wailings of a thousand ghosts on your coat-trails!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T14:54:38-07:00","id":862202,"title":"","content":"<b>Spirit-Lightening Confessional</b><br /> The deathknight brings release to those who no longer wish to bear the burden of knowledge. This Charm supplements a dramatic action during which the character interviews, interrogates, or otherwise extracts knowledge from another through spoken language.<br /> <br /> As the person speaks, his words are transcribed upon a surface of the character's choosing - vellum, parchment, or even clay tablets are common choices. The words appear as sooty arcane figures legible only to those conversant in the secret languages of the dead. Once the transcription is complete, the knowledge so dictated will fade and vanish from the mind of the speaker over the course of a few hours - faint recollections of having once known something now forgotten are all that remain. This may also erode or destroy associated Intimacies, if this is appropriate. So long as the transcription exists the subject can never know what he has spoken again, even if it is later imparted to him by another. Where the knowledge once resided, there is only forgetfulness. Only by reading the original transcription can the speaker regain the knowledge and memories taken from him.<br /> <br /> At Essence 3+, the character can designate a repository for such knowledge in a sanctum with which she is connected. This may take a number of forms: a specially-prepared tome, a stone plinth, or some other surface appropriate to receive the knowledge he gathers. The deathknight may elect to have the transcribed words appear on the designated surface, regardless of distance. Some Abyssals maintain repositories of stolen lore, forever lost to those who once knew it.<br /> <br /> (Evil librarian for the win!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T16:19:48-07:00","id":862257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/861738-growlscampaigncraft-abyssals-and-linguistics-brainstorm-ideas-welcome?p=861804#post861804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woah there... you have 4 Solar PCs and the one caste that wasn't taken was Twilight? That's pretty shocking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was surprised too. But the Dawn is pretty twilighty. He's a Sorcerer, all about overcoming challenges and his sorcery is a tool for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T17:51:03-07:00","id":862306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/861738-growlscampaigncraft-abyssals-and-linguistics-brainstorm-ideas-welcome?p=861766#post861766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> The Dead's Language - Being able to communicate with and command (even mindless) undead, regardless of their languages in life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssals already get this in Infinite Blasphemy Glossolalia, except with any Creature of Darkness.<br /> <br /> They also get some fairly good sized telepathy in the form of Screaming in Silence(100xlinguistics yards) for anything and (Linguistics) miles for any Creatures of Death in Voiceless Horror Mastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}